Z||000005||AkursedX||06-20-2001||09:15 PM||||Here's a list of small cubic feet (under.6 cubic feet of space) subs that i could find.  (these are all sealed measurements)<P>Polk DX 8inch-.33 (cubic feet)<BR>sony xplod 8inch-.5<BR>Infinity Kappa and Perfect 10inch-.6<BR>Kenwood small box 10 inch-.6<BR>Pioneer VCCS Pro 10 inch- .6<BR>Sony Xplod ES 10 inch-.6<P>Rockford Fosgate Punch Z 8" and 10", Punch HE 8" and 10", Punch HE2 8" and 10" and Punch HX2 8"and 10" are all under or at .6 cubic feet<P>MTX audio Thunder 4000 8inch- .38-.88<BR>MTX audio Thunder 4000 6000 and 8000 series 10 inch woofers are all under or at .6 cubic feet<P>Kicker Comp VR 8 inch sub- .4-1.8<P>Hope this list helps.  I got all this info from crutchfield, and I'm sure there are some better subwoofers out there.  <P>My personal Favorite is the Infinity Perfect 10".  Nice and tight and clear.  I wish I had the money to afford one when I was looking.  It probably won't win any bassoffs though, but it'll give excellent sound.||||reg||1
Z||000006||grinthock||06-20-2001||09:18 PM||||Hmmm did some looking (Hey AkursedX!, email me dude!)<P>Here is what I found out<P>What I am looking for is a sub for the AusFieroBOX<P>10" sub...  We have .6 to play with.<P>OZ 10"  0.75 - 1.50 cu.ft<BR>Sony XS-L106SG 10" DVC  .6  ($239)<BR>(sony makes a bunch for small box)<BR>Pioneer VCCS Pro TS-W2541DVC  .6  ($199)<BR>Kicker Solo-Baric S10L7  .66  ($299)<BR>RF Punch HE2 RFP3210 0.375-1.75 ($174.95)<P> After looking all this CRAP over, a DVC sub is probably the way I would go, any audio nuts wanna tell me a reason why DVC is bad I would like to hear it!  So far I like the Sony, it's not TOO TOO expensive (all prices were crutchfield USD) it's nice looking (yeah looks matter because with AUS Fiero's box it's all exposed!)<P>Something with a Sensitivity of 85 is crappy though! I have seen cheap $80 subs with a sensitivity of 90+  why is this?  All the good subs are always low sens...  There are cheaper options though. Due to small space and sealed, power is gonna be required to drive it....<P><p>[This message has been edited by grinthock (edited 06-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||grinthock||06-20-2001||09:21 PM||||geez we posted over each other... I like that Sony-ES 10"..... Sounds like a good idea....  Looks good too (as an added bonus but I wish I had the RED INTERIOR TO MATCH LIKE AUS!)||||reg||1
Z||000008||Huck||06-20-2001||10:59 PM||||I have a JL Audio 10W3 Dual 2ohm that rocks.  Its just in a footwell fiberglass enclosure right now, so it doesn't do it complete justice (I actually cracked the box a bit right after I put it in).  I have had it in a real box too though, and it really does pound.. I'll let you know how it sounds in the AUS-box that I ordered tonight!<BR>Minimum enclosure size is 0.5, and recommended it 0.65 so it should work good.  Its a dual voice coil (dual 2ohm) and Im running it at4ohms.  I truly believe it is the right, and only way to go.  In ontairo, it retails for $400 canadian, but I picked one up for $230 at a liquidation sale.<P>Huck||||reg||1
Z||000009||Neverfinished||06-20-2001||11:40 PM||||I just picked up a 10inch Concept for 230 canadian and it just pounds...<BR>DVC in a .57cf box that i made for the footwell. Don't port the box! If you are running enough power then keep it sealed!<BR>Concept subs kick a$$<P>------------------<BR>To Be Old And Wise, You First Must Be Young And Stupid.-----------------<BR>It's not a waste of time... If you are wasted at the time||||reg||1
Z||000010||1FST2M6||06-21-2001||08:14 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.velodyne.com" TARGET=_blank>www.velodyne.com</A>  , <A HREF="http://www.xtant.com" TARGET=_blank>www.xtant.com</A>  , <A HREF="http://www.klipsch.com" TARGET=_blank>www.klipsch.com</A>   but i've found the Kicker Solo L7s to be the best for my SE... take .3 with ease and that saying a lot for 10" sub. pulled a 38 out of 40 in the Q (frequency performance range test)and slammed to 141db on the SPL meter. but the velodyne is just as nice and will take more abuse. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||grinthock||06-21-2001||06:27 PM||||I think I found the sub!!!  Good price too<P>Rockford Fosgate 10" DVC HE2<BR>It's a $169 Canadian which is not too bad (That's 95-100 USD)<BR>Works in a .3 -- &gt; 1.00 Cubic box, and I heard one in a small box sounded great.<P>Aus Will this guy fit?  It's almost 6 inches deep!||||reg||1
